ess(b),\n        \"log_len\":''')\ns=s.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(''','''    streak_diff = pm.Data(\"streak_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_len = pm.Data(''')\ns=s.replace('''    # The change: shared penalty on a rule-built''','''    # The change: shared penalty per flip of the longest streak beyond two.\n    delta = pm.HalfNormal(\"delta\", sigma=1.0)\n\n    # Shared penalty on a rule-built''')\ns=s.replace('''    # The change: person-specific pattern''','''    # Person-specific pattern''')\ns=s.replace('''        + side[participant_id]''','''        - delta * streak_diff\n        + side[participant_id]''')\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nPY\ncat > $C/model_name.txt <<'EOF'\nstreak_excess_pattern_rule_built\nEOF\ncat > $C/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of the incumbent `person_pattern_sensitivity_rule_built` (running heads-minus-tails tally judged by closeness of its span to a personal expected span with person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity; switching judged by closeness to an ideal rate with a person-specific weight; a reward for three-flip chunk variety and a penalty on rule-built sequences, both scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity; a personal left/right lean). The one change: people treat a long streak of identical flips as a salient sign of non-randomness in its own right — every flip of the longest run beyond two (HHH, HHHH, ...) counts against a sequence, in absolute flips rather than as a share of its length — a shared streak penalty taken from the pruned streak models (`periodic_ideal_absolute_streak_penalty`). Of two sequences with the same tally span, switching rate and chunk structure, people pick the one whose longest streak is shorter, including on pairs where pattern structure cannot act, where the incumbent predicts indifference.\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && grep -n \"streak\\|delta\\|The change\" $C/candidate.py && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin